<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gabrielle (Hootenanny Singers)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1964</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Immer lebe die Sonne (Ilse and Hans Naumilkat, Manfred Streubel)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation (German)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Paistaa aurinko aina</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation (Finnish)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Olgu jääv meile päike (Heljo Mänd; recorded by Georg Ots)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation (Estonian)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hebrew version (Gidi Koren; The Brothers &amp; the Sisters)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new Hebrew words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Together in Concert (Pete Seeger and Arlo Guthrie)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1975</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in English</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">10 Carrot Diamond (Charlotte Diamond)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1985</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chorus sung in six languages</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Let's Play (Raffi)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">chorus sung in English, Spanish and French</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Opening ceremony of the 2014 Winter Olympics, Sochi</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2014</span><span class="sg-chain-h">part of a medley</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Monument to Samantha Smith, Artek</span><span class="sg-chain-h">title inscribed on the pedestal</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Four lines by Kostya Barannikov (aged four)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1928</span><span class="sg-chain-h">refrain, according to Korney Chukovsky</span></li></ul></section>
